{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides the cleanest possible single-variable comparison: it changes only the modality while holding profile_setting=singleprofile constant and using a standard, well-understood encoder (resnet50) to avoid confounding training instability. If image accuracy substantially exceeds or falls below the RNA baseline, we immediately know whether to prioritize multimodal fusion or invest in improving the RNA encoder/aggregation. If they are similar, we learn that neither modality alone is sufficient and multimodal fusion becomes the key lever. This is the highest-information experiment under a limited budget because it resolves the most consequential design question (which modality to build on) before spending further experiments on encoder or aggregation variants within a single modality."
}

